---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How Often Should You Recheck Your Bra Size? | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Learn how often to re-measure your bra size. Discover how weight shifts, hormonal changes, fitness, and elastic breakdown change bra fit over time."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/guides/how-often-to-measure-bra-size"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Guides', url: '/#guides' },
      { label: 'Rechecking Bra Size' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Evergreen Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        How Often Should You Recheck Your Bra Size?
      </h1>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-mute mb-4">
        <span>By BraSizeChecker Editorial Team</span>
        <span>&bull;</span>
        <time datetime="2026-08-24">Updated August 2026</time>
      </div>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Most people wear the same bra size for years without realizing their body measurements have shifted. Here is the recommended schedule for rechecking your size.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <section class="bg-canvas-soft-2 border-2 border-primary/30 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">Recommended Schedule: Every 6 to 12 Months</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Lingerie experts recommend taking your measurements <strong>every 6 to 12 months</strong>, or whenever you experience significant lifestyle or body changes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Key Triggers to Re-Measure Immediately</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">1. Weight Fluctuations (&plusmn; 5-10 lbs)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Ribcage underbust fat and breast tissue are often among the first places to reflect weight shifts.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">2. Post-Pregnancy or Nursing Shifts</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Ribcage expansion during pregnancy and glandular density changes post-nursing alter band and cup requirements.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">3. Fitness & Muscle Changes</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Developing latissimus dorsi or pectoral muscles from strength training increases underbust width while altering cup projection.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Bra Lifespan & Elastic Degradation</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Even if your body doesn't change, bras degrade over time. A bra worn regularly lasts approximately <strong>6 to 9 months</strong> before the band elastic loses recoil and requires replacement.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/how-to-measure" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-primary text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-primary-hover shadow-2xs">Re-Measure at Home &rarr;</a>
          <a href="/#calculator" class="px-5 py-2.5 bg-surface border border-hairline text-ink font-semibold text-xs rounded-xl hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 shadow-2xs">Calculate New Size &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
